# No em dashes in page text

Do not use em dashes (`—`, Unicode U+2014) in user-facing portfolio copy.

This applies to content in `content/`, page components in `app/`, metadata titles/descriptions, headings, body copy, CTAs, and labels.

## Use instead

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `clause—clause` | Comma: `clause, clause` |
| `intro—detail` | Colon: `intro: detail` |
| `Label — value` | Middle dot: `Label · value` |
| Separate sentences | Period: `sentence. Sentence` |
| Parenthetical aside | Commas: `text, aside, text` |

## Examples

```
// Bad
"Built for production—not prototypes."
"Production MVP — direct or POC-first"
"You came here from my proposal—this page was the proof."

// Good
"Built for production, not prototypes."
"Production MVP · direct or POC-first"
"You came here from my proposal. This page was the proof."
```

## Notes

- Middle dots (`·`) are fine for labels, tags, and separators.
- Hyphens (`-`) in compound words and en dashes in numeric ranges are fine.
- Upwork client quotes must stay verbatim; do not edit quoted text to remove em dashes.
